f paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   in this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  the results of immunohistochemical staining for progesterone receptor protein are for investigational use only  they must not be used for clinical purposes  added by  frederick carl koerner  m d  signed on  08 aug 94 at 07 18 gross description  received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled remove_patient_name  patient s name  unit number  and  left   is a removed_date x removed_date x 2 0cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue with localizing wire and accompanying mammogram  the specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a white  firm nodule  measuring removed_date x 0 5cm with irregular borders that approach the resection margin  sections of this nodule are submitted in a through e  other suspicious regions submitted in f through j  resident  edwin s  monuki  md     intra operative diagnosis     gross diagnosis  breast left   no gross tumor identified  o r  resident  stamatina kaptain  md o r  diagnosis by  max l  goodman  m d                                                                                  source care unit  surgical day care   acc 3 reports to  herbert charles hoover jr   m d  part   left breast   report_end  , Yes.
