accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  finaltype  surgical pathology pathology report   removed_accession_id  operation date  02 removed_month 01 accessioned on  03 removed_month 01 at 09 41 clinical data  dcis on excisional biopsy  comedo type                                                                                       final diagnosis     breast  right   modified radical mastectomy  1  ductal carcinoma in situ  predominately grade 1 with focal grade 2  spanning at least removed_date cm and located far away from margins  2  metastatic carcinoma in 1 of 15 axillary lymph nodes  see note  3  one intraparenchymal lymph node free of carcinoma  4  complex sclerosing lesion  5  fibrocystic changes  6  healing biopsy site  note  the metastatic deposits in the lymph node aggregate to  0 1cm and consist of cohesive  whorled epithelial cell clusters located in the subcapsular sinuses  their epithelial nature is confirmed by positive cytokeratin immunostaining  the slightly spindled morphology of the cells and the nuclear atypia are histologically similar to areas of the patient s ductal carcinoma in situ  despite extensive examination and thorough sampling of the mastectomy specimen  no invasive carcinoma is found in the breast parenchyma itself  review of the patient s prior biopsy specimens does not reveal any invasive component  drs  dennis sgroi and ben pilch have reviewed selected slides and concur with the diagnosis of metastatic carcinoma  the ductal carcinoma in situ demonstrates a prominent spindle cell morphology in many areas  and there is also focal comedonecrosis  a grimelius stain is negative for argyrophilic granules  stains for er  pr  and her 2 neu will be attempted on the remaining lymph node tissue and will be reported in an addendum  diagnosis by  melinda j  fan  md signed on  16 removed_month 01 at 17 57                                                                                     immunohistochemistry addendum     results o